[ASK: How to go to a packet given a certain time?](https://ask.wireshark.org/question/37274/how-to-go-to-a-packet-given-a-certain-time/)  

@jvalverde  `time_is_negative` is not checking `value.time.nsecs` so `abs()` not working for negative time values less than a whole second.  

Should it be  
`return (fv->value.time.secs < 0 || fv->value.time.nsecs < 0);`  
or  
`return (fv->value.time.secs + fv->value.time.nsecs) < 0;`

[epan/ftypes/ftype-time.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/ftypes/ftype-time.c#L537):  
```
static bool
time_is_negative(const fvalue_t *fv)
{
	return fv->value.time.secs < 0;
}

static enum ft_result
time_unary_minus(fvalue_t * dst, const fvalue_t *src, char **err_ptr _U_)
{
	dst->value.time.secs = -src->value.time.secs;
	dst->value.time.nsecs = -src->value.time.nsecs;
	return FT_OK;
}
```

